---
scope: "A ComposeUX widget that HOSTS a PTY-backed interactive `claude` session inside a ComposeApp, so the Intelligence Console can launch and host an Intelligence with NO Terminal.app, NO AppleScript, and no dependence on macOS. Covers why the two alternatives (an `osascript` Terminal spawn; `--print --output-format stream-json` headless) were REJECTED; the THREE candidate target modes for V1 (`tui: fullscreen`, `tui: default`, `--ax-screen-reader`) and the rule that V1's target is CHOSEN FROM THE CENSUS, not assumed; the escape-sequence census that is the first build task and its validity conditions; the PTY half reused by reference from `launcher.py`; the `pyte` dependency decision; the ONE sequence table shared by the census tool and the runtime degradation detector; the render/input halves the engine is missing; damage scoping + the coalescing cadence; the error/boundary matrix; and the two-tier acceptance bar."
audience: "The builder implementing the census, the terminal widget and the launcher PTY-core extraction; the composeux-architect ratifying the open calls (V1's target mode, pyte, the host surface, Tab capture, the launcher-singleton ownership); anyone who later asks why the console does not just shell out to Terminal.app, or why it does not run `claude -p`."
boundary: "IN: the rejected alternatives and their evidence ([CXC-TERM-REJECT-TERMINAL], [CXC-TERM-REJECT-HEADLESS], [CXC-TERM-FACTS]); the three candidate target modes and the choose-from-measurement rule ([CXC-TERM-SCOPE], [CXC-TERM-AXMODE], [CXC-TERM-PIN]); the census as a gating build task ([CXC-TERM-CENSUS], [CXC-TERM-SEQTABLE], [CXC-TERM-HYPOTHESIS]); the PTY core extraction + winsize/SIGWINCH ([CXC-TERM-PTYCORE], [CXC-TERM-WINSIZE]); the singleton collision ([CXC-TERM-SINGLETON]); the emulator + renderer + input map ([CXC-TERM-EMULATOR], [CXC-TERM-GRID], [CXC-TERM-INPUT], [CXC-TERM-PASTE]); the widget + its registry descriptor + every default ([CXC-TERM-WIDGET]); the dialog rule ([CXC-TERM-DIALOGS]); damage + cadence ([CXC-TERM-DAMAGE]); visible degradation ([CXC-TERM-DEGRADE]); the boundary matrix and the acceptance bar. Added by the FIRST LIVE SPAWN (2026-08-11): the hosted child's DISTINCT identity and the three symptoms one shared id produced ([CXC-TERM-CHILD-ID]); manifest resolution as a CHAIN that refuses loudly ([CXC-TERM-MANIFEST-CHAIN]); the child's own context telemetry, reusing the launcher's EXISTING monitor ([CXC-TERM-CHILD-TELEMETRY]); bootstrap delivery on ARGV and the DELETION of the settle-delay injection path ([CXC-TERM-BOOTSTRAP-ARGV], [CXC-TERM-BOOTSTRAP-SETTLE-RETIRED]); clipboard paste as one branch on the existing input path ([CXC-TERM-INPUT]); the census's configuration-fidelity rule ([CXC-TERM-CENSUS-CONFIG-FIDELITY]). OUT: `tui: fullscreen` support, which is V2 whichever target V1 picks ([CXC-TERM-SCOPE], migration path stated); the `/compact` actuation relay's own semantics ([CXC-IC-LIFECYCLE] — consumed, never changed); the harness monitor's OWN semantics ([CXC-IC-MONITOR] — REUSED unchanged; only the widget's WIRING of it is in scope, [CXC-TERM-CHILD-TELEMETRY]); the fleet spawner ([CXC-IH-HOST]); the console's launch AFFORDANCE and its presence rule, which are [SPEC:CXC-IC-LAUNCH]'s and survive this spec unchanged ([CXC-TERM-SUPERSEDES-55])."
not-this: "Not a general-purpose terminal emulator — V1 targets exactly ONE program (`claude`, in ONE measured mode chosen per [CXC-TERM-SCOPE]) and its supported-sequence set is DERIVED FROM A MEASUREMENT of that program ([CXC-TERM-CENSUS]), not from a standards document. Not a spec that assumes the favourable census answer — [CXC-TERM-HYPOTHESIS] is explicitly UNCONFIRMED, both prior probe attempts are VOID ([CXC-TERM-CENSUS-PRIOR]), and the build has a defined branch for a refutation. Not a fork of `launcher.py` — the PTY half is EXTRACTED to a shared module both callers import ([CXC-TERM-PTYCORE]); a second `pty.fork()` + `select` loop in the tree is a review reject ([DX-NARROW-WAIST]). Not an auto-answered startup dialog — keystroke injection into Claude Code's startup dialogs was tried, collided with the human, and hung ([CXC-TERM-DIALOGS]); it stays out of scope forever, exactly as in [CXC-ICL-CONSTRAINT-PTY]. Not a replacement for [SPEC:CXC-IC-LAUNCH] — that spec's intent, id validation, peer guard, cold-start rule and pane swap all SURVIVE; only its terminal-spawn MECHANISM is retired ([CXC-TERM-SUPERSEDES-55]). Not a headless-mode port — `-p` cannot express `/compact` and is disqualified permanently ([CXC-TERM-REJECT-HEADLESS])."
